# Runtime dependencies for the Lambda functions. This file is the sole input to
# the shared dependency layer, and the layer has a hard 262144000 byte unzipped
# limit, so keep it to what lambda/src actually imports. Test, lint and security
# tooling belongs in ../requirements-test.in.
#
# Every entry below is imported by lambda/src:
#   arnparse, aws_xray_sdk, boto3, botocore, requests  - all handlers
#   eks_token, kubernetes                              - EKS support in
#                                                        triage/app.py and
#                                                        isolation/isolateEc2.py
arnparse==0.0.2
aws-xray-sdk==2.15.0
boto3==1.43.73
botocore==1.43.73
eks-token==0.3.0
# Pinned below 36.x deliberately. 36.0.0 added an asyncio client
# (kubernetes.aio) plus a hard aiohttp dependency, which costs 54 MB of layer
# budget for functionality this solution does not use: triage/app.py and
# isolation/isolateEc2.py only use the synchronous `client` and `config` APIs.
# 35.0.0 is the newest release without the async client, and every version from
# 31 to 36 is free of known advisories, so there is no security cost.
kubernetes==35.0.0
requests==2.34.2
urllib3==2.7.0
